---
import LandingLayout from '../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/landing/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/landing/Footer.astro';
import { contacts } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'November 2, 2026';
---

<LandingLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Artifact Keeper"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Artifact Keeper server, web interface, demo instance and Cloud waitlist."
>
  <Navbar solid current="/privacy/" />

  <main id="top" class="page">
    <article class="legal wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="pip"></span>Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how Artifact Keeper ("we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and shares
        information when you use our software and services, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Artifact Keeper Server (self-hosted)</li>
        <li>Artifact Keeper Web Interface</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>Self-Hosted Server</h3>
      <p>
        Artifact Keeper Server is designed to be self-hosted on your own infrastructure. When you run
        Artifact Keeper Server:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>We do not collect any data.</strong> All data remains on your servers under your control.</li>
        <li>No telemetry, analytics, or usage data is sent to us.</li>
        <li>No network requests are made to our servers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Web Interface</h3>
      <p>
        The web interface is served by your own Artifact Keeper installation and talks only to that server.
        It does not include third-party analytics or advertising scripts and does not send data to us.
      </p>

      <h3>Demo Instance</h3>
      <p>
        If you use our public demo instance at demo.artifactkeeper.com:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Basic server logs (IP addresses, timestamps) may be collected for security and abuse prevention.</li>
        <li>Any artifacts you upload to the demo are visible to other demo users and may be periodically deleted.</li>
        <li>Do not upload sensitive or private data to the demo instance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cloud Waitlist</h3>
      <p>
        If you join the <a href="/cloud/">Artifact Keeper Cloud waitlist</a>, we keep the email address
        (and the company name, if you give one) that you submit.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The address is used only to announce Artifact Keeper Cloud and to send occasional product updates.</li>
        <li>Signups are stored with GetWaitlist (getwaitlist.com), and delivered by FormSubmit (formsubmit.co) to <span class="addr">{contacts.support}</span> as a fallback.</li>
        <li>You can unsubscribe from any email, or ask us to remove you by writing to <a href={`mailto:${contacts.support}`}>{contacts.support}</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>
        For self-hosted installations and the web interface, we do not collect or use any of your information.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the demo instance, server logs may be used to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Monitor for abuse and security threats</li>
        <li>Debug technical issues</li>
        <li>Understand general usage patterns (not individual behavior)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Self-hosted:</strong> You are responsible for securing your own Artifact Keeper installation.
        We recommend following the security best practices in our <a href="/docs/">documentation</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        Artifact Keeper does not integrate with third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking services.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you configure SSO authentication (LDAP, OIDC, SAML), your Artifact Keeper server will communicate
        with your identity provider according to your configuration.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Artifact Keeper is a developer tool intended for use by software development professionals.
        Our services are not directed at children under 13 years of age, and we do not knowingly collect
        personal information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Since we do not collect personal data from self-hosted installations, there is no personal data
        for us to provide, correct, or delete.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the demo instance and the Cloud waitlist, you may contact us to request deletion of any data
        associated with your use.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by
        posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Open Source</h2>
      <p>
        Artifact Keeper is open source software. You can review our code to verify our privacy practices:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper">Server</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper-web">Web Interface</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:privacy@artifactkeeper.com">privacy@artifactkeeper.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Or open an issue on our <a href="https://github.com/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper/issues">GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</LandingLayout>
